---
import Layout from '@/layouts/Layout.astro';
import { getLegalInfo } from '@/lib/legal';

// SSR so the controller contact can be read from the runtime environment.
export const prerender = false;

const legal = getLegalInfo();
const lastUpdated = '16 August 2026';
Astro.response.headers.set('Cache-Control', 'public, max-age=300, s-maxage=3600');
---
<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy - DRepTalk"
  description="How DRepTalk handles your data. Wallet-based, data-minimal, no tracking."
  noindex={true}
>
  <article class="legal">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal__meta">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

    <p>
      DRepTalk is a wallet-authenticated forum for Cardano governance, built around
      data minimization. We use no passwords, no email accounts, and no third-party
      advertising or cross-site tracking. This policy explains what we process and
      your rights under the GDPR.
    </p>

    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>
      The controller responsible for data processing on this site is:<br />
      {legal.operatorName}<br />
      {legal.addressLines.map((line) => (<>{line}<br /></>))}
      Email: <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>
    </p>

    <h2>What we process, and why</h2>

    <h3>Wallet sign-in and identity</h3>
    <p>
      Authentication is non-custodial. You prove control of a Cardano wallet by signing
      a one-time message; we never receive, request, or store private keys, and there
      is no password. When you sign in, we store your public on-chain identifier (for
      example your DRep ID or stake address) and the on-chain role it proves (DRep, SPO,
      Constitutional Committee member, or proposer) in order to grant posting access.
      You can also sign in as a delegator: in that case we store your stake address and
      the delegation it currently points to (for example the DRep you delegate to),
      refreshed periodically from public chain data, in order to show your delegation
      dashboard and to enable the optional notifications described below.
      Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (providing the service you request) and (f)
      (legitimate interest in operating a forum with verifiable on-chain roles).
    </p>

    <h3>Content you publish</h3>
    <p>
      Topics, posts, and reactions you create are public and are stored, attributed to
      your public on-chain identifier. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) and (f) GDPR.
    </p>

    <h3>Session cookie</h3>
    <p>
      We set one strictly necessary cookie to keep you signed in. We set no advertising
      or tracking cookies, so no consent banner is required. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f)
      GDPR and &sect; 25(2) TDDDG (strictly necessary).
    </p>

    <h3>Notifications (optional)</h3>
    <p>
      If you enable browser push notifications, we store the push subscription your
      browser issues (its endpoint URL and the public encryption key for that device)
      together with your per-event preferences, and use it to deliver notifications.
      Delivery necessarily runs through the push service of your browser vendor (for
      example Google, Mozilla, or Apple). Notification content is end-to-end encrypted
      (RFC 8291): we encrypt each notification with that public key, the matching
      private key never leaves your browser, and the push service cannot read the
      content and only handles delivery metadata. You can disable push at any time in your notification settings or in
      your browser, which removes the subscription. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR
      (consent).
    </p>
    <p>
      If you link a Telegram account, we store your Telegram chat ID and send
      notifications through the Telegram Bot API. Unlike push, the content of these
      messages is visible to Telegram, as with any Telegram message. You can unlink
      Telegram at any time in your notification settings, which deletes the stored
      chat ID. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(a) GDPR (consent).
    </p>

    <h3>Server logs and security</h3>
    <p>
      Our hosting and security provider (Cloudflare) processes connection data such as
      your IP address to deliver the site, defend against abuse, and rate-limit
      requests. These are retained only briefly. Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR
      (security and reliable operation).
    </p>

    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      The site uses Cloudflare Web Analytics, a privacy-preserving,
      cookieless tool that collects only aggregate metrics. It does not use cookies,
      does not fingerprint you, and does not track you across sites. Legal basis:
      Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR.
    </p>

    <h3>Public blockchain data</h3>
    <p>
      To verify your role and to show governance information and DRep profiles, we read
      public data from the Cardano blockchain through the Koios API. We do not transmit
      personal data to Koios beyond public on-chain identifiers. Profile details (name,
      description, image) that DReps publish on-chain via CIP-119 are displayed here;
      profile images are served through our own cache, so your browser never contacts
      the third-party hosts these images come from and your IP address is not revealed
      to them.
    </p>

    <h2>Recipients and processors</h2>
    <p>
      We do not sell your data and use no third-party advertising or tracking. We rely
      on:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Cloudflare, Inc.: hosting, content delivery, security, and cookieless analytics, under a data processing agreement.</li>
      <li>Koios: a public, read-only Cardano data API; we send only public on-chain identifiers.</li>
      <li>Browser push services (Google, Mozilla, or Apple, depending on your browser): deliver the push notifications you enable; content is end-to-end encrypted, so they handle only delivery metadata.</li>
      <li>Telegram: delivers notifications if you link a Telegram account; these messages are readable by Telegram.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Some processing (for example over Cloudflare's global network) may take place
      outside the EU/EEA, safeguarded by the EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Account data is kept while your account is active. Public content remains part of
      the forum record until it is removed. When a post is deleted it disappears from the
      forum at once, and once 30 days have passed its text is erased from our database,
      along with every earlier version of it and its search index entry. If a whole thread
      is deleted, this erases every post in it, but the thread's title is not erased: it
      stays in the thread's web address and in our search index indefinitely. The 30 days
      exist so that abuse reports about a removed post can still be dealt with. Backups held
      by our hosting provider are overwritten on their own schedule and are not used to
      restore deleted content. Connection and security
      logs are kept only briefly. Data written to the public Cardano blockchain (for
      example a DRep registration you submit) is outside our control and cannot be
      deleted by us.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Under the GDPR you have the right of access (Art. 15), rectification (Art. 16),
      erasure (Art. 17), restriction (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20), and
      objection (Art. 21), and the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory
      authority. To exercise these, contact us at
      <a href={`mailto:${legal.email}`}>{legal.email}</a>. We can remove your forum
      account and content, but we cannot alter or erase data recorded on the public
      blockchain.
    </p>

    <h2>Automated decision-making</h2>
    <p>We do not use automated decision-making or profiling within the meaning of Art. 22 GDPR.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>We may update this policy. The current version is always available on this page.</p>
  </article>

  <style>
    .legal {
      max-width: 46rem;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 1rem 0 4rem;
      line-height: 1.7;
    }
    .legal h1 {
      font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 4vw, 2.2rem);
      margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    }
    .legal__meta {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
    }
    .legal h2 {
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      margin: 2rem 0 0.5rem;
    }
    .legal h3 {
      font-size: 1rem;
      margin: 1.25rem 0 0.35rem;
    }
    .legal p,
    .legal li {
      color: var(--fg);
    }
    .legal p {
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
    }
    .legal ul {
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      padding-left: 1.25rem;
    }
    .legal li {
      margin: 0 0 0.35rem;
    }
    .legal a {
      color: var(--accent);
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
